{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000301",
  "title": "Conformal Maps",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "description": "Visualize how holomorphic functions transform grids in the complex plane while preserving angles between curves.",
  "tags": [
    "complex-analysis",
    "visualization",
    "math"
  ],
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Conformal Maps\n\nA **conformal map** is a function that preserves angles between curves at every point where it is defined. In complex analysis, any **holomorphic** (complex-differentiable) function $f(z)$ is conformal wherever its derivative $f'(z) \\neq 0$.\n\n## What \"Angle-Preserving\" Means\n\nIf two curves cross at a point $z_0$ forming angle $\\theta$, their images under $f$ cross at $f(z_0)$ at the *same* angle $\\theta$. The curves may be stretched, compressed, or bent \u2014 but the angle at each intersection is preserved.\n\n## Why Holomorphic Implies Conformal\n\nA holomorphic function $f$ acts locally like multiplication by $f'(z_0)$, which is a nonzero complex number. Multiplying by a complex number $r e^{i\\alpha}$ scales by $r$ and rotates by $\\alpha$ \u2014 neither operation changes the angle between two vectors. When $f'(z_0) = 0$, the local behavior is degenerate and angles can be multiplied (e.g., $f(z) = z^2$ doubles angles at the origin).\n\n## This Notebook\n\nEach visualization below shows:\n- **Left panel**: A rectangular grid in the input domain (horizontal lines in warm colors, vertical lines in cool colors)\n- **Right panel**: The same grid after transformation by $f(z)$\n\nHorizontal and vertical lines meet at 90\u00b0 in the input. Under a conformal map, the transformed curves \u2014 even though they may be warped \u2014 still cross at 90\u00b0 everywhere $f'(z) \\neq 0$.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Scaling and Rotation",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Scaling and Rotation: $f(z) = az$, $a = 2e^{i\\pi/4}$\n\nThe simplest conformal map: multiplication by a constant $a = 2e^{i\\pi/4}$.\n\n- **Geometric effect**: Every point is scaled by $|a| = 2$ (distances double) and rotated by $\\arg(a) = \\pi/4 = 45\\degree$.\n- **Derivative**: $f'(z) = a \\neq 0$ everywhere, so the map is conformal on the entire plane.\n- **Grid behavior**: Straight lines stay straight. The grid is uniformly scaled and rotated \u2014 a rigid similarity transformation. Angles are trivially preserved because the transformation is linear.\n\nThis is the \"base case\" \u2014 every holomorphic function looks like this locally (at non-critical points).",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "f(z) = az",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\nuse std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst N: usize = 11;\nconst S: usize = 400;\n\nfn draw_seg(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let (dx, dy) = ((x1 - x0).abs(), -(y1 - y0).abs());\n    let (sx, sy) = (if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 }, if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 });\n    let (mut e, mut x, mut y) = (dx + dy, x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * e;\n        if e2 >= dy { e += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { e += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn map_pt(vx: f64, vy: f64, d: (f64, f64, f64, f64), p: (f64, f64, f64, f64)) -> (i32, i32) {\n    let (dw, dh) = (d.1 - d.0, d.3 - d.2);\n    let scale = if dw > 0.0 && dh > 0.0 { (p.2 / dw).min(p.3 / dh) } else { 1.0 };\n    ((p.0 + p.2 / 2.0 + (vx - (d.0 + d.1) / 2.0) * scale) as i32,\n     (p.1 + p.3 / 2.0 - (vy - (d.2 + d.3) / 2.0) * scale) as i32)\n}\n\n// f(z) = 2e^(i\u03c0/4) \u00b7 z  \u2014 scale by 2, rotate 45\u00b0\nlet a_re = 2.0_f64 * (PI / 4.0).cos();\nlet a_im = 2.0 * (PI / 4.0).sin();\nlet f = |re: f64, im: f64| -> (f64, f64) {\n    (a_re * re - a_im * im, a_re * im + a_im * re)\n};\nlet dom = (-2.0_f64, 2.0, -2.0, 2.0);\n\n// Compute output bounds (2nd\u201398th percentile for robustness)\nlet mut xs: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nlet mut ys: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    for j in 0..S {\n        let s = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let pts = [\n            f(dom.0 + s * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n            f(dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + s * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n        ];\n        for &(px, py) in pts.iter() {\n            if px.is_finite() && py.is_finite() {\n                xs.push(px);\n                ys.push(py);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\nxs.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nys.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nlet n = xs.len();\nlet lo = n / 50;\nlet hi = n - 1 - n / 50;\nlet mx = (xs[hi] - xs[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet my = (ys[hi] - ys[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet out = (xs[lo] - mx, xs[hi] + mx, ys[lo] - my, ys[hi] + my);\n\nlet left = (5.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet right = (410.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\ncanvas.fill((10, 10, 25));\n\nfor py in 0..H {\n    canvas.set_pixel(397, py, (35, 35, 55));\n    canvas.set_pixel(398, py, (35, 35, 55));\n}\n\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, dom, left);\nif ax.0 >= 5 && ax.0 < 390 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 5u32..390 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, out, right);\nif ax.0 >= 410 && ax.0 < 795 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 410u32..795 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\n\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    let hc = ((180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, 50);\n    let vc = (50, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, (180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8);\n    let yv = dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2);\n    let xv = dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0);\n\n    for j in 0..S - 1 {\n        let s0 = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let s1 = (j + 1) as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n\n        // Horizontal line segment\n        let (a, b) = (dom.0 + s0 * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.0 + s1 * (dom.1 - dom.0));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(a, yv, dom, left), map_pt(b, yv, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(a, yv), f(b, yv));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Vertical line segment\n        let (a, b) = (dom.2 + s0 * (dom.3 - dom.2), dom.2 + s1 * (dom.3 - dom.2));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(xv, a, dom, left), map_pt(xv, b, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(xv, a), f(xv, b));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_3",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Squaring",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Squaring: $f(z) = z^2$\n\n- **Geometric effect**: Squares the modulus ($|z|^2$) and doubles the argument ($2\\arg z$). Circles centered at the origin map to circles; rays from the origin map to rays at double the angle.\n- **Derivative**: $f'(z) = 2z$, which vanishes at $z = 0$. Conformality breaks down at the origin \u2014 angles there are **doubled** rather than preserved.\n- **Grid behavior**: Horizontal and vertical lines map to parabolas. Away from the origin, these parabolas still cross at right angles. Near the origin, the grid lines pinch together and the angle-doubling is visible.\n\nThe right panel shows the characteristic parabolic grid of $z^2$. Notice how the transformed curves still meet at 90\u00b0 everywhere except at the image of the origin.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_4",
      "order": 4,
      "label": "f(z) = z^2",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\nuse std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst N: usize = 11;\nconst S: usize = 400;\n\nfn draw_seg(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let (dx, dy) = ((x1 - x0).abs(), -(y1 - y0).abs());\n    let (sx, sy) = (if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 }, if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 });\n    let (mut e, mut x, mut y) = (dx + dy, x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * e;\n        if e2 >= dy { e += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { e += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn map_pt(vx: f64, vy: f64, d: (f64, f64, f64, f64), p: (f64, f64, f64, f64)) -> (i32, i32) {\n    let (dw, dh) = (d.1 - d.0, d.3 - d.2);\n    let scale = if dw > 0.0 && dh > 0.0 { (p.2 / dw).min(p.3 / dh) } else { 1.0 };\n    ((p.0 + p.2 / 2.0 + (vx - (d.0 + d.1) / 2.0) * scale) as i32,\n     (p.1 + p.3 / 2.0 - (vy - (d.2 + d.3) / 2.0) * scale) as i32)\n}\n\n// f(z) = z\u00b2\nlet f = |re: f64, im: f64| -> (f64, f64) {\n    (re * re - im * im, 2.0 * re * im)\n};\nlet dom = (-1.5_f64, 1.5, -1.5, 1.5);\n\nlet mut xs: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nlet mut ys: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    for j in 0..S {\n        let s = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let pts = [\n            f(dom.0 + s * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n            f(dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + s * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n        ];\n        for &(px, py) in pts.iter() {\n            if px.is_finite() && py.is_finite() {\n                xs.push(px);\n                ys.push(py);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\nxs.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nys.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nlet n = xs.len();\nlet lo = n / 50;\nlet hi = n - 1 - n / 50;\nlet mx = (xs[hi] - xs[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet my = (ys[hi] - ys[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet out = (xs[lo] - mx, xs[hi] + mx, ys[lo] - my, ys[hi] + my);\n\nlet left = (5.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet right = (410.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\ncanvas.fill((10, 10, 25));\n\nfor py in 0..H {\n    canvas.set_pixel(397, py, (35, 35, 55));\n    canvas.set_pixel(398, py, (35, 35, 55));\n}\n\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, dom, left);\nif ax.0 >= 5 && ax.0 < 390 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 5u32..390 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, out, right);\nif ax.0 >= 410 && ax.0 < 795 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 410u32..795 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\n\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    let hc = ((180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, 50);\n    let vc = (50, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, (180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8);\n    let yv = dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2);\n    let xv = dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0);\n\n    for j in 0..S - 1 {\n        let s0 = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let s1 = (j + 1) as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.0 + s0 * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.0 + s1 * (dom.1 - dom.0));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(a, yv, dom, left), map_pt(b, yv, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(a, yv), f(b, yv));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n            }\n        }\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.2 + s0 * (dom.3 - dom.2), dom.2 + s1 * (dom.3 - dom.2));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(xv, a, dom, left), map_pt(xv, b, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(xv, a), f(xv, b));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_5",
      "order": 5,
      "label": "Exponential",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Exponential: $f(z) = e^z$\n\n- **Geometric effect**: $e^{x+iy} = e^x(\\cos y + i\\sin y)$. Horizontal lines (constant $y$) map to **rays** from the origin at angle $y$. Vertical lines (constant $x$) map to **circles** of radius $e^x$. The rectangular grid becomes a polar grid.\n- **Derivative**: $f'(z) = e^z \\neq 0$ for all $z$, so the map is conformal everywhere.\n- **Domain**: We use $[-2, 2] \\times [-\\pi, \\pi]$ so the imaginary axis covers one full period.\n\nThe right panel shows the classic rectangular-to-polar transformation. Every intersection in the polar grid maintains a perfect 90\u00b0 crossing \u2014 rays and circles are always perpendicular.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_6",
      "order": 6,
      "label": "f(z) = e^z",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\nuse std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst N: usize = 11;\nconst S: usize = 400;\n\nfn draw_seg(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let (dx, dy) = ((x1 - x0).abs(), -(y1 - y0).abs());\n    let (sx, sy) = (if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 }, if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 });\n    let (mut e, mut x, mut y) = (dx + dy, x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * e;\n        if e2 >= dy { e += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { e += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn map_pt(vx: f64, vy: f64, d: (f64, f64, f64, f64), p: (f64, f64, f64, f64)) -> (i32, i32) {\n    let (dw, dh) = (d.1 - d.0, d.3 - d.2);\n    let scale = if dw > 0.0 && dh > 0.0 { (p.2 / dw).min(p.3 / dh) } else { 1.0 };\n    ((p.0 + p.2 / 2.0 + (vx - (d.0 + d.1) / 2.0) * scale) as i32,\n     (p.1 + p.3 / 2.0 - (vy - (d.2 + d.3) / 2.0) * scale) as i32)\n}\n\n// f(z) = e^z\nlet f = |re: f64, im: f64| -> (f64, f64) {\n    let r = re.exp();\n    (r * im.cos(), r * im.sin())\n};\nlet dom = (-2.0_f64, 2.0, -PI, PI);\n\nlet mut xs: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nlet mut ys: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    for j in 0..S {\n        let s = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let pts = [\n            f(dom.0 + s * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n            f(dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + s * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n        ];\n        for &(px, py) in pts.iter() {\n            if px.is_finite() && py.is_finite() {\n                xs.push(px);\n                ys.push(py);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\nxs.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nys.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nlet n = xs.len();\nlet lo = n / 50;\nlet hi = n - 1 - n / 50;\nlet mx = (xs[hi] - xs[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet my = (ys[hi] - ys[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet out = (xs[lo] - mx, xs[hi] + mx, ys[lo] - my, ys[hi] + my);\n\nlet left = (5.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet right = (410.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\ncanvas.fill((10, 10, 25));\n\nfor py in 0..H {\n    canvas.set_pixel(397, py, (35, 35, 55));\n    canvas.set_pixel(398, py, (35, 35, 55));\n}\n\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, dom, left);\nif ax.0 >= 5 && ax.0 < 390 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 5u32..390 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, out, right);\nif ax.0 >= 410 && ax.0 < 795 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 410u32..795 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\n\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    let hc = ((180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, 50);\n    let vc = (50, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, (180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8);\n    let yv = dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2);\n    let xv = dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0);\n\n    for j in 0..S - 1 {\n        let s0 = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let s1 = (j + 1) as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.0 + s0 * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.0 + s1 * (dom.1 - dom.0));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(a, yv, dom, left), map_pt(b, yv, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(a, yv), f(b, yv));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n            }\n        }\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.2 + s0 * (dom.3 - dom.2), dom.2 + s1 * (dom.3 - dom.2));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(xv, a, dom, left), map_pt(xv, b, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(xv, a), f(xv, b));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_7",
      "order": 7,
      "label": "Logarithm",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Logarithm: $f(z) = \\ln(z)$ (principal branch)\n\n- **Geometric effect**: The inverse of the exponential. $\\ln(z) = \\ln|z| + i\\arg(z)$. Circles centered at the origin map to **vertical lines**, and rays from the origin map to **horizontal lines**. A polar grid becomes rectangular \u2014 the exact reverse of $e^z$.\n- **Derivative**: $f'(z) = 1/z$, which is nonzero for all $z \\neq 0$. Conformal everywhere except the origin.\n- **Branch cut**: The principal branch has a discontinuity along the negative real axis. We restrict the domain to $[0.2, 3] \\times [-2.5, 2.5]$ (right half-plane) to avoid the branch cut and the singularity at $z = 0$.\n\nNotice how the output grid is nearly rectangular \u2014 the logarithm \"straightens\" the radial structure of the input domain.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_8",
      "order": 8,
      "label": "f(z) = ln(z)",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\nuse std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst N: usize = 11;\nconst S: usize = 400;\n\nfn draw_seg(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let (dx, dy) = ((x1 - x0).abs(), -(y1 - y0).abs());\n    let (sx, sy) = (if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 }, if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 });\n    let (mut e, mut x, mut y) = (dx + dy, x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * e;\n        if e2 >= dy { e += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { e += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn map_pt(vx: f64, vy: f64, d: (f64, f64, f64, f64), p: (f64, f64, f64, f64)) -> (i32, i32) {\n    let (dw, dh) = (d.1 - d.0, d.3 - d.2);\n    let scale = if dw > 0.0 && dh > 0.0 { (p.2 / dw).min(p.3 / dh) } else { 1.0 };\n    ((p.0 + p.2 / 2.0 + (vx - (d.0 + d.1) / 2.0) * scale) as i32,\n     (p.1 + p.3 / 2.0 - (vy - (d.2 + d.3) / 2.0) * scale) as i32)\n}\n\n// f(z) = ln(z) (principal branch)\nlet f = |re: f64, im: f64| -> (f64, f64) {\n    let r = (re * re + im * im).sqrt();\n    if r < 1e-10 { return (f64::NAN, f64::NAN); }\n    (r.ln(), im.atan2(re))\n};\nlet dom = (0.2_f64, 3.0, -2.5, 2.5);\n\nlet mut xs: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nlet mut ys: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    for j in 0..S {\n        let s = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let pts = [\n            f(dom.0 + s * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n            f(dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + s * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n        ];\n        for &(px, py) in pts.iter() {\n            if px.is_finite() && py.is_finite() {\n                xs.push(px);\n                ys.push(py);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\nxs.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nys.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nlet n = xs.len();\nlet lo = n / 50;\nlet hi = n - 1 - n / 50;\nlet mx = (xs[hi] - xs[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet my = (ys[hi] - ys[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet out = (xs[lo] - mx, xs[hi] + mx, ys[lo] - my, ys[hi] + my);\n\nlet left = (5.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet right = (410.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\ncanvas.fill((10, 10, 25));\n\nfor py in 0..H {\n    canvas.set_pixel(397, py, (35, 35, 55));\n    canvas.set_pixel(398, py, (35, 35, 55));\n}\n\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, dom, left);\nif ax.0 >= 5 && ax.0 < 390 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 5u32..390 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, out, right);\nif ax.0 >= 410 && ax.0 < 795 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 410u32..795 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\n\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    let hc = ((180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, 50);\n    let vc = (50, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, (180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8);\n    let yv = dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2);\n    let xv = dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0);\n\n    for j in 0..S - 1 {\n        let s0 = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let s1 = (j + 1) as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.0 + s0 * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.0 + s1 * (dom.1 - dom.0));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(a, yv, dom, left), map_pt(b, yv, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(a, yv), f(b, yv));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n            }\n        }\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.2 + s0 * (dom.3 - dom.2), dom.2 + s1 * (dom.3 - dom.2));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(xv, a, dom, left), map_pt(xv, b, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(xv, a), f(xv, b));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_9",
      "order": 9,
      "label": "Complex Sine",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Complex Sine: $f(z) = \\sin(z)$\n\n- **Geometric effect**: $\\sin(x + iy) = \\sin(x)\\cosh(y) + i\\cos(x)\\sinh(y)$. Vertical lines (constant $x$) map to **hyperbolas**, and horizontal lines (constant $y$) map to **ellipses**. These conic sections share foci at $\\pm 1$ on the real axis.\n- **Derivative**: $f'(z) = \\cos(z)$, which vanishes at $z = \\pm\\pi/2 + n\\pi$. Conformality breaks down at these critical points.\n- **Domain**: $[-\\pi, \\pi] \\times [-2, 2]$ covers one full period in the real direction.\n\nThe output shows the elegant confocal ellipse/hyperbola grid. Near $z = \\pm\\pi/2$ (where $\\cos(z) = 0$), the grid lines pinch together and angles are distorted.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_10",
      "order": 10,
      "label": "f(z) = sin(z)",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\nuse std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst N: usize = 11;\nconst S: usize = 400;\n\nfn draw_seg(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let (dx, dy) = ((x1 - x0).abs(), -(y1 - y0).abs());\n    let (sx, sy) = (if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 }, if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 });\n    let (mut e, mut x, mut y) = (dx + dy, x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * e;\n        if e2 >= dy { e += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { e += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn map_pt(vx: f64, vy: f64, d: (f64, f64, f64, f64), p: (f64, f64, f64, f64)) -> (i32, i32) {\n    let (dw, dh) = (d.1 - d.0, d.3 - d.2);\n    let scale = if dw > 0.0 && dh > 0.0 { (p.2 / dw).min(p.3 / dh) } else { 1.0 };\n    ((p.0 + p.2 / 2.0 + (vx - (d.0 + d.1) / 2.0) * scale) as i32,\n     (p.1 + p.3 / 2.0 - (vy - (d.2 + d.3) / 2.0) * scale) as i32)\n}\n\n// f(z) = sin(z)\nlet f = |re: f64, im: f64| -> (f64, f64) {\n    (re.sin() * im.cosh(), re.cos() * im.sinh())\n};\nlet dom = (-PI, PI, -2.0_f64, 2.0);\n\nlet mut xs: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nlet mut ys: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    for j in 0..S {\n        let s = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let pts = [\n            f(dom.0 + s * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n            f(dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + s * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n        ];\n        for &(px, py) in pts.iter() {\n            if px.is_finite() && py.is_finite() {\n                xs.push(px);\n                ys.push(py);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\nxs.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nys.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nlet n = xs.len();\nlet lo = n / 50;\nlet hi = n - 1 - n / 50;\nlet mx = (xs[hi] - xs[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet my = (ys[hi] - ys[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet out = (xs[lo] - mx, xs[hi] + mx, ys[lo] - my, ys[hi] + my);\n\nlet left = (5.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet right = (410.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\ncanvas.fill((10, 10, 25));\n\nfor py in 0..H {\n    canvas.set_pixel(397, py, (35, 35, 55));\n    canvas.set_pixel(398, py, (35, 35, 55));\n}\n\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, dom, left);\nif ax.0 >= 5 && ax.0 < 390 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 5u32..390 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, out, right);\nif ax.0 >= 410 && ax.0 < 795 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 410u32..795 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\n\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    let hc = ((180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, 50);\n    let vc = (50, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, (180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8);\n    let yv = dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2);\n    let xv = dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0);\n\n    for j in 0..S - 1 {\n        let s0 = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let s1 = (j + 1) as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.0 + s0 * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.0 + s1 * (dom.1 - dom.0));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(a, yv, dom, left), map_pt(b, yv, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(a, yv), f(b, yv));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n            }\n        }\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.2 + s0 * (dom.3 - dom.2), dom.2 + s1 * (dom.3 - dom.2));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(xv, a, dom, left), map_pt(xv, b, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(xv, a), f(xv, b));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_11",
      "order": 11,
      "label": "Mobius Transformation",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## M\u00f6bius Transformation: $f(z) = \\frac{z - 1}{z + 1}$\n\nM\u00f6bius transformations (linear fractional transformations) are the most important conformal maps in complex analysis. They map circles and lines to circles and lines.\n\n- **Geometric effect**: This particular M\u00f6bius map sends $z = 1 \\mapsto 0$, $z = -1 \\mapsto \\infty$, and $z = 0 \\mapsto -1$. It maps the right half-plane to the unit disk.\n- **Derivative**: $f'(z) = \\frac{2}{(z+1)^2}$, which is nonzero for all $z \\neq -1$. Conformal everywhere except the pole.\n- **Key property**: M\u00f6bius transformations are the *only* bijective conformal maps of the Riemann sphere to itself.\n\nNear $z = -1$ (the pole), grid lines blow up to infinity. The percentile-based scaling prevents these outliers from dominating the visualization. Notice how the transformed grid lines curve but always maintain 90\u00b0 crossings.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_12",
      "order": 12,
      "label": "f(z) = (z-1)/(z+1)",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\nuse std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst N: usize = 11;\nconst S: usize = 400;\n\nfn draw_seg(c: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, col: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let (dx, dy) = ((x1 - x0).abs(), -(y1 - y0).abs());\n    let (sx, sy) = (if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 }, if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 });\n    let (mut e, mut x, mut y) = (dx + dy, x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && x < W as i32 && y >= 0 && y < H as i32 {\n            c.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, col);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * e;\n        if e2 >= dy { e += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { e += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn map_pt(vx: f64, vy: f64, d: (f64, f64, f64, f64), p: (f64, f64, f64, f64)) -> (i32, i32) {\n    let (dw, dh) = (d.1 - d.0, d.3 - d.2);\n    let scale = if dw > 0.0 && dh > 0.0 { (p.2 / dw).min(p.3 / dh) } else { 1.0 };\n    ((p.0 + p.2 / 2.0 + (vx - (d.0 + d.1) / 2.0) * scale) as i32,\n     (p.1 + p.3 / 2.0 - (vy - (d.2 + d.3) / 2.0) * scale) as i32)\n}\n\n// f(z) = (z - 1) / (z + 1)  \u2014 M\u00f6bius transformation\nlet f = |re: f64, im: f64| -> (f64, f64) {\n    let d = (re + 1.0) * (re + 1.0) + im * im;\n    if d < 1e-10 { return (f64::NAN, f64::NAN); }\n    ((re * re + im * im - 1.0) / d, 2.0 * im / d)\n};\nlet dom = (-2.0_f64, 2.0, -2.0, 2.0);\n\nlet mut xs: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nlet mut ys: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    for j in 0..S {\n        let s = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let pts = [\n            f(dom.0 + s * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n            f(dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.2 + s * (dom.3 - dom.2)),\n        ];\n        for &(px, py) in pts.iter() {\n            if px.is_finite() && py.is_finite() {\n                xs.push(px);\n                ys.push(py);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\nxs.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nys.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());\nlet n = xs.len();\nlet lo = n / 50;\nlet hi = n - 1 - n / 50;\nlet mx = (xs[hi] - xs[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet my = (ys[hi] - ys[lo]) * 0.05;\nlet out = (xs[lo] - mx, xs[hi] + mx, ys[lo] - my, ys[hi] + my);\n\nlet left = (5.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet right = (410.0_f64, 5.0, 385.0, 390.0);\nlet mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\ncanvas.fill((10, 10, 25));\n\nfor py in 0..H {\n    canvas.set_pixel(397, py, (35, 35, 55));\n    canvas.set_pixel(398, py, (35, 35, 55));\n}\n\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, dom, left);\nif ax.0 >= 5 && ax.0 < 390 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 5u32..390 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nlet ax = map_pt(0.0, 0.0, out, right);\nif ax.0 >= 410 && ax.0 < 795 {\n    for py in 5u32..395 { canvas.set_pixel(ax.0 as u32, py, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\nif ax.1 >= 5 && ax.1 < 395 {\n    for px in 410u32..795 { canvas.set_pixel(px, ax.1 as u32, (30, 30, 50)); }\n}\n\nfor i in 0..N {\n    let t = i as f64 / (N - 1) as f64;\n    let hc = ((180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, 50);\n    let vc = (50, (50.0 + 130.0 * t) as u8, (180.0 + 75.0 * t) as u8);\n    let yv = dom.2 + t * (dom.3 - dom.2);\n    let xv = dom.0 + t * (dom.1 - dom.0);\n\n    for j in 0..S - 1 {\n        let s0 = j as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n        let s1 = (j + 1) as f64 / (S - 1) as f64;\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.0 + s0 * (dom.1 - dom.0), dom.0 + s1 * (dom.1 - dom.0));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(a, yv, dom, left), map_pt(b, yv, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(a, yv), f(b, yv));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, hc);\n            }\n        }\n\n        let (a, b) = (dom.2 + s0 * (dom.3 - dom.2), dom.2 + s1 * (dom.3 - dom.2));\n        let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(xv, a, dom, left), map_pt(xv, b, dom, left));\n        draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n        let (ta, tb) = (f(xv, a), f(xv, b));\n        if ta.0.is_finite() && ta.1.is_finite() && tb.0.is_finite() && tb.1.is_finite() {\n            let (p0, p1) = (map_pt(ta.0, ta.1, out, right), map_pt(tb.0, tb.1, out, right));\n            if (p0.0 - p1.0).abs() + (p0.1 - p1.1).abs() < 100 {\n                draw_seg(&mut canvas, p0.0, p0.1, p1.0, p1.1, vc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ]
}
